==Trivia==
*Internally, the '''Star Wars Skins''' are actually an unobtainable ''Star Wars Crate'' which has the same model as the [[Basic Crate]].
**The crate itself is set to be [[Daily Store]] only, which when combined with its appearance suggests it is not meant to be obtainable and should only function like the [[Content Creator Skins]], which is also a crate.
*Both skins present as part of this skin series were made for the 4th of May 2024, which is the [[wp:Star Wars Day|Star Wars Day]].
**The description of the crate which cannot be seen anywhere in-game references this event.
**When the skins were made unobtainable once the 4th of May 2024 ended, it was mentioned that the developers had plans for them in the future. It is likely them appearing in the [[Daily Store]] is that plan.<ref>[[File:StarWarsSkinsPlanProof.png|280px]]<br/>https://discord.com/channels/587355301083349002/664997359071002637/1237143962075136161 (Tower Defense Simulator Server)</ref>
*While the skin series and the crate it is internally is referred to as ''Star Wars'', it does not actually contain every ''Star Wars'' skin in the game.
**There is a {{Color|Deluxe|Galactic}} [[Gladiator]] skin that can be obtained from the [[Deluxe Crate]]. It is meant to represent [[w:c:starwars:Sith Lord|Sith Lord]], though its design does not match any specific one.
**The [[Warden]] has a {{Color|Deluxe|Galactic}} skin that is also obtained from the [[Deluxe Crate]]. The skin is based on the [[w:c:starwars:Stormtroopers|Stormtroopers]].
**The {{Color|Mission|Trooper}} [[Commando]] skin is obtained from [[Mission Quests]]. It is based on [[w:c:starwars:Clone commando|Clone commandos]] from ''Star Wars''.

